@node Getting Started
@chapter Getting Started

To compile a C file using @command{gcc}, pass the source filename and specify an output binary with @option{-o}.

@example
gcc -Wall -O2 hello.c -o hello
./hello
@end example

See @ref{Command Options} for details on modifying behavior.

@node Command Options
@chapter Command Options

You can customize the output by passing @var{filename} to the @code{process_file} function.

@table @code
@item --verbose
Prints detailed execution steps to standard output.

@item --output=@var{file}
Writes the result to @var{file} instead of the terminal.
@end table

@bye
